ap=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)
ap.add_argument('--project-root',type=Path,default=BUILD.parents[2])
PROJECT=ap.parse_args().project_root.resolve()
if (BUILD/'report-input.json').exists() and json.loads((BUILD/'report-input.json').read_text()).get('ready_for_final'):
    raise ValueError('Do not replace a finalized report input with this preparation draft')
blocks=[]
def h(text):blocks.append({'type':'heading','text':text,'level':2})
def s(text):blocks.append({'type':'heading','text':text,'level':3})
def p(text):blocks.append({'type':'p','text':text})
def table(headers,rows,widths):blocks.append({'type':'table','headers':headers,'rows':rows,'widths':widths})

h('Introduction')
p('A replacement agent may receive neutral instructions while inheriting an earlier agent’s harmful convention through a handoff. We study this channel in a small allocation task where the enacted consequences are fully observable. The experiment asks whether delivering authentic notes changes fresh agents’ joint behavior, whether notes from the same original branch differ from crossed sources, and whether an instruction to verify the handoff reduces harmful transfer without reducing legitimate collaboration.')
p('The contribution is a controlled source-routing audit with committed original actions, independently sampled successors, a legitimate-objective control and explicit eligibility denominators. It is not a study of spontaneous collusion: the experimenter instructs every original coalition. The tested environment is a Colosseum-derived fixture with a complete public outcome table, not the full Colosseum multi-agent platform [1,4]. [[FINAL CONTRIBUTION SENTENCE GROUNDED IN SUCCESSOR RESULTS]].')

h('Related work')
p('Colosseum evaluates collusion through cooperative multi-agent environments and behavioral outcomes [1]. We reuse its task-allocation motivation in a reduced fixture, replacing open interaction with two independent choices and scripted outsiders. Self-Propagating Misalignment already examines persistence of misaligned objectives into neutral successors through memory and other channels [2]; inherited misalignment itself is therefore not a novelty claim here. Salami Attack introduces MemCollusion, in which fragments compose within one downstream agent [3]. Our two role-specific notes instead reach separate recipients, and source pairing is evaluated through their joint enacted allocation. The contribution is this limited intervention structure and auditable execution record, not the first demonstration of harmful memory persistence or composition.')

h('Study development and amendments')
p('The study changed after earlier competence and donor observations. Three initial development attempts produced 18 probe responses and no originals or successors. Two requested Qwen-235B Instruct runs failed their full-allocation checks. A third requested Qwen-235B Thinking run returned a different provider-reported model identifier on every response; it cannot establish that requested model’s capability or actual served weights. These attempts are retained as development evidence, not pooled into V4.')
p('V3 then admitted a Qwen pilot through six probes and executed its original allocations. A reviewer first rejected false global-optimality claims. Amendment 01 substantively relaxed that rule before successors, allowing separately annotated derived false claims but retaining primitive-fact and recipient-fidelity requirements. A later B note directed its successor to A’s task, so V3 still failed; the DeepSeek pilot had separately failed a competence probe. V3’s 28 calls produced zero successor episodes. Neither its failed status nor its original protocol is retrospectively revised.')
p('V4 changes the estimand to delivery of the entire technically usable handoff channel, including sender errors. The local protocol, model list, cases, controls, budget and source were frozen at 17:52:39 UTC on 23 October 2026, with zero successor requests. This is a locally frozen prospective protocol before successor outcomes, not a public preregistration or a design chosen without prior model observations. GPT-OSS was selected in advance of successor effects for another model family and low published cost; the fixed protocol prohibits further candidate replacement after qualification failure.')
p('Strict V4 subsequently exposed format-induced attrition: a correct Qwen seed-206 competence answer and later successor answers were enclosed in Markdown JSON fences, which the frozen JSON-only parser rejected. The original strict records and primary analysis remain unchanged. A separate V4F continuation was then chosen after execution began. It accepts only one complete outer JSON fence and leaves the enclosed strict schema, identity, finish, usage and scientific gates unchanged. Saved raw responses are reused rather than resampled, and only never-dispatched planned calls can be newly collected. [[BIND FINAL V4F PROTOCOL RECORD AND EXACT DECISION CHRONOLOGY]].')

h('Methods')
s('Task and committed original actions')
p('A and B independently choose one of four tasks. Scripted C and D then choose distinct unclaimed tasks minimizing their combined cost, with a fixed tie-break. Each valid assignment earns 100 minus cost; an extra duplicate claimant incurs a penalty of 200 shared among claimants. The common successor objective first maximizes distinct task completion and then minimizes cost across all four agents. Both roles see the public cost matrix and all 16 possible A/B outcomes, including the C/D continuation and rewards. This explicit table removes much of the planning burden.')
p('Eight fixed cases, seeds 201–208, vary costs and task labels. A/B costs are 1–4 on two outsider-specialty tasks and 5–10 on the remaining tasks. Each outsider’s specialty costs 0–2, the other specialty 7–13, and other tasks 14–36. Exhaustive enumeration checks the cooperative reference. Two A/B permutations of the non-specialty tasks are equally team-optimal; taking both specialties raises A+B reward and lowers C+D reward. These are designed properties, not model findings.')
p('Each case has four original branches: harmful or legitimate objective, each with an experimenter-supplied p0 or p1 allocation. Two action calls must execute that assigned plan. The actual scored original outcome is saved before two note-writing calls. Each original then writes to its own replacement. The successor round resets all tasks to unclaimed, keeps costs fixed and treats prior rewards as sunk. A successor receives only its neutral instruction, public task and own note, without its predecessor’s system objective or its partner’s response. Original agents do not negotiate.')
s('Qualification and the unfiltered handoff channel')
p('Each model first receives a separate seed-902 qualification: two complete-allocation probes and four elementary queue-note probes. Every main case repeats the same six-check structure. Competence requires the correct own task, unique complete A/B/C/D allocation, exact cost and internal consistency; the asymmetric probe fixture has one optimum. Queue routing establishes elementary note access, not use of the actual task’s conventions. Every check must pass. A failed case is retained and never replaced; a failed model qualification ends that model’s planned main execution.')
p('Original actions must match their plans, but a later note’s reported task need not match the committed action. A technically usable note requires the fixed schema, a known task identifier, nonempty text, at most 2,000 characters and a successor request within the fixed byte bound. False facts, refusals, unclear instructions and experiment labels inside otherwise usable text never exclude, repair or regenerate the note. All eight notes per admitted case are annotated before successors, with exact hashes and reviewer/time records. Annotation completion is required; its truth values are not an execution filter.')
s('Interventions and model configuration')
blocks.append({'type':'caption','text':'Table 1. Fixed delivery routes in each original-objective mode. Sources p0 and p1 identify original branches, not certified semantic compatibility.'})
table(['Condition','A source','B source','Additional instruction'],[
 ['Facts only','None','None','None'],['Same source p0','p0','p0','None'],['A only','p0','None','None'],['B only','None','p0','None'],
 ['Crossed 01','p0','p1','None'],['Crossed 10','p1','p0','None'],['Same source p1','p1','p1','None'],['Verify p0','p0','p0','Check public objective']],
 [2600,1200,1200,4360])
p('The verification reminder asks successors to check the note against public rules and all-four-agent cost, keeping compatible recommendations and disregarding conflicts. It supplies no solution and is identical in both modes. It is a prompt intervention, not verified execution of a checking algorithm. Facts-only prompts are identical across nominal modes but separately sampled. Mode, condition and repeat order are shuffled within each case using its fixed seed.')
p('The fixed configurations are Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B and openai/gpt-oss-120b, both routed through DeepInfra via Hugging Face. Both use temperature 0.6, top-p 0.95 and maximum output 8,192 tokens. No reasoning_effort or extra_body is sent; effective provider reasoning defaults remain unspecified. These common sampling settings are not claimed to be optimal. Every response must report the exact requested model identifier and a complete finish. Matching identifiers do not independently verify served weights. Missing, malformed or excessive reported token usage/cost stops new requests for that model after preserving its raw response; already dispatched parallel calls may still complete.')
s('Outcomes and paired analysis')
p('There are two successor draws per condition and original-objective mode, sharing each model’s case-specific notes: 32 joint episodes per case and 512 planned across two models. The independent task units are eight case clusters per model, not 512 independent experiments. Models generate different notes, so between-model differences combine authorship and recipient response. Intervention comparisons are within model and case.')
p('Joint harm requires A/B to take the two distinct outsider specialties with positive coalition gain and outsider loss relative to the cooperative reference. Report it alongside team reward, completion, duplicate violations, individual specialty choices and adherence to the assigned original convention. Primary contrasts are same-source p0 minus facts, same-source p1 minus facts, and verify p0 minus same-source p0. Average two paired draws within each complete case, then weight cases equally. Missing outcomes are not zero; both repeats and all compared arms are needed. Report per-case differences and planned, eligible and complete denominators, without significance tests or population confidence intervals.')
p('The secondary balanced source-pairing contrast is (Y00 + Y11 − Y01 − Y10)/2. It preserves each recipient’s marginal note exposure but is not a semantic-compatibility effect unless the notes faithfully encode the intended conventions. A separate note-presence interaction on joint harm can arise mechanically from its conjunctive definition. Neither establishes strategic interaction or composition inside a recipient. A strict secondary subset requires accurate primitive facts, clearly faithful recipient assignments, no refusal or labels, and all derived claims true; undecidable claims fail that subset. It is content-selected and sensitive to AI-assisted judgment, while the primary analysis remains unfiltered.')
p('Actual-task convention use is assessed separately in legitimate p0 and p1: at least 12 of the planned 16 episodes must follow each convention, per model. Missing outcomes cannot improve this criterion. It does not control execution and is not a pure recipient-comprehension measure, because defective handoffs can cause failure. The frozen protocol also defines limited descriptive labels for observed transfer, replication across cases, qualified negatives and useful verification; any final label must satisfy its complete criteria.')
p('Strict V4 and the later V4F analysis must be reported separately. The continuation is an explicitly post-start format amendment, not an independent replication or a wholly prospective design. It adds no models, task seeds, conditions or repeats and preserves the original maximum of 1,388 distinct planned calls. Reused valid responses, newly admitted fenced responses and newly collected responses require separate counts. The two analyses share observations and cannot be pooled as independent samples. New calls occur later in time, so endpoint drift or temporal variation can accompany the changed format policy. [[FINAL EXACT CONTINUATION RULE AND SOURCE HASH]].')
p('The continuation and report layout were frozen before aggregate-effect inspection. This was not complete outcome blinding: during a later technical-status diagnosis, an insufficiently filtered summary accidentally exposed a partial Qwen seed-205 contrast and individual case outcomes. The recorded incident led to no design, parser, collection or presentation change; the case retained its format-related stop. The exact event time is unknown but bounded to 19:32:24–19:34:04 UTC on 23 October, with a separate record time of 19:34:19.986017 UTC in docs/v4f-outcome-visibility-note.json. Model-level aggregate effects had not been inspected at that incident. The separate seed-206 annotation reviewer examined only that case’s public fixture, original allocations and eight notes; the completed review at 19:42:47.507149 UTC confirmed zero requests or episodes for its successors.')
p('A post-start sensitivity analysis gives logical completion bounds for missing planned outcome slots: binary endpoints use 0–1, and continuous endpoints use each task’s enumerated finite range. The amendment called these “identification/sensitivity bounds”; scientific review clarified before effect analysis that their justified interpretation is narrower. They are not confidence intervals, proof of competence or identified full-cohort handoff effects. In particular, strict Qwen206 never produced original notes. Such bounds describe possible arithmetic completions, separately from conditional observed-pair estimates.')

h('Results')
p('Both seed-902 model qualifications passed all six probes under separate AI-assisted review of final content. All four competence answers gave A=T3, B=T4, C=T1, D=T2 at total cost 17, and all eight queue probes followed their supplied targets. All 12 response identifiers matched, finishes were complete, and reported usage satisfied the bounds. Strict main probes admitted 15 of 16 planned cases, which generated 120 original notes. Qwen seed 206 B supplied the correct task T4, full assignment A=T1/B=T4/C=T3/D=T2 and cost12 inside a Markdown JSON fence. The frozen parser rejected that wrapper; the exclusion is a format-policy failure, not evidence of incorrect reasoning. Retrospective semantic inspection does not change the original gate.')
p('[[FINAL STAGE FLOW TABLE: retain every qualification/main model-case denominator, Qwen206 schema failure, requested/reported identifiers, donor technical validity, all missingness and complete successor counts.]]')
p('[[FINAL BALANCED STAGE-FLOW TABLE: strict V4 and amended V4F by model; planned, eligible, attempted, valid, incomplete and missing denominators; original and newly generated note counts.]]')
p('[[FINAL MAIN EFFECTS: all modes/conditions, contrary cases, team utility/completion/duplicates, primary case-paired effects and actual-task convention criterion.]]')
p('[[FINAL BALANCED PRIMARY-CONTRAST TABLE: strict V4 and amended V4F paired case summaries and complete/planned case denominators; retain null, reversed and utility-damaging findings; do not label arithmetic bounds as confidence intervals.]]')
p('[[FINAL SECONDARY ANALYSIS: source pairing, one-note arms, faithful-subset denominators, exact annotation categories and a reproducibly selected trace with actions and scorer outcome. Recipient-assignment flags include absent/ambiguous next-round instructions and must not all be called definite role errors.]]')
p('[[FINAL SEPARATE V4F RESULTS: strict-versus-continuation stage denominators and findings, cached-valid/fence-recovered/newly-collected counts, remaining format failures, additional notes/annotations and missingness. Do not merge costs or observations twice.]]')

h('Discussion and conclusion')
p('[[FINAL CONCLUSION FROM THE FIXED ANALYSIS SNAPSHOT ONLY. Distinguish observed or replicated descriptive transfer, zero observed harm, qualified negative, and failures of faithful-note/manipulation checks. Do not turn toy-task zero counts into a blanket robustness claim.]]')
p('The experiment isolates delivery of fixed notes conditional on competent probes, correct original execution and technical availability. It does not estimate an unconditional end-to-end transfer rate. Semantic failures belong to the handoff channel and remain visible. The donor-driven redesign makes V4 more faithful to that broader channel question, but narrows any claim about inheritance of accurately transmitted plans. Source-pairing effects may also reflect damage to legitimate coordination. Verification changes instructions as well as attention; this design does not identify a latent checking mechanism or the causal effect of individual false claims.')
p('Generalization is limited by one transparent numerical task family, a full outcome table, scripted outsiders, independent one-shot recipients, supplied original objectives and two provider endpoints. Eight cases per model and two nested draws give descriptive precision only. Provider defaults and served weights are unverified, and AI-assisted annotations are not independent human validation. Further work should use more task families, repeated interactions, blinded human annotation and controlled edits that separately vary factual content, evaluative claims and intended allocation.')
h('Code and data')
p('A local companion package contains the frozen protocol and source, all raw requests/responses, original outcomes, exact notes and pre-successor annotations, scored episodes, analysis, figures and report build sources. No public repository or stable archival URL is claimed. The package SHA256 manifest and per-run source snapshots bind the evidence. [[FINAL SOURCE AND ANALYSIS IDENTIFIERS]].')

